<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:54:41 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Revisiting the delicate art of French patisserie</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261027-revisiting-the-delicate-art-of-french-patisserie</link><description>
In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet Nour Kandler, a self-taught pastry chef whose approach to French patisserie is shaped by a deep appreciation for its traditions and the rich flavours of her Middle Eastern heritage. She shares her unique perspective on pastry, where classic French techniques intertwine with cultural influences to create a style that is both personal and distinctive.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e97c98e-d20a-11f1-bd76-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5758065c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0e97c98e-d20a-11f1-bd76-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5758065c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4ad10cc4-d207-11f1-80a1-5d84579d7797</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:45:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Israeli election: A referendum on 'Bibi' Netanyahu?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261027-israeli-election-a-referendum-on-bibi-netanyahu</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 27: The Israeli, Palestinian and Lebanese papers break down what's at stake on election day for Israel and its neighbours. Also, the French government announces its first major concessions to protesting high school students, hoping to calm the movement. Finally, Harry Kane's Ballon d'Or means Lamine Yamal and Kylian Mbappé will have to wait their turn.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bb98da0-d1f2-11f1-a2cb-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4622d283.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0bb98da0-d1f2-11f1-a2cb-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4622d283.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4d57b80a-d1e2-11f1-8eac-491f57832fb0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:52:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli PM casts his ballot as voters voice opposition to Netanyahu outside polling stations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-pm-casts-his-ballot-as-voters-voice-opposition-to-netanyahu-outside-polling-stations</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu cast his vote on Tuesday (October 27) in Israel’s general election. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7986d44c-d200-11f1-b046-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-120101-120452-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7986d44c-d200-11f1-b046-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-120101-120452-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">83d0f054-d200-11f1-b0c3-e105dc525688</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:42:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>England's Kane wins Ballon d'Or, Putellas claims women's award</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/england-s-kane-wins-ballon-d-or-putellas-claims-women-s-award</link><description>
Harry Kane completed his long quest ⁠for football's highest individual ​honour on Monday (October 26), the Bayern Munich and England striker winning the Ballon d'Or after a record-breaking season that cemented his status as one of the game's greatest goalscorers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e222ec3e-d200-11f1-8678-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-121123-121259-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e222ec3e-d200-11f1-8678-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-121123-121259-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e797e0d4-d200-11f1-b45b-b3d8c5599583</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:37:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Localised Russia-Ukraine ceasefire starts Ukrainian town facing starvation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-localised-russia-ukraine-ceasefire-starts-ukrainian-town-facing-starvation</link><description>
A localised ceasefire between Ukraine and Russia took effect early Tuesday (October 27) ahead of a humanitarian mission led by US first lady Melania Trump, as missile attacks resumed in Kyiv. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Kyiv, Emmanuelle Chaze, has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eda218e8-d1a4-11f1-9062-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/37d1dc6b018faa3403f2a1f253bd0bc47e1a1ebe.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eda218e8-d1a4-11f1-9062-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/37d1dc6b018faa3403f2a1f253bd0bc47e1a1ebe.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">360e782c-d1fc-11f1-9903-8f0754652aee</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:34:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'Get the Flock out': Americans respond to AI cameras in bipartisan backlash</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-united-states-get-the-flock-out-americans-respond-to-ai-cameras-in-bipartisan-backlash-midterm-elections</link><description>
AI-driven Flock cameras made by an Atlanta-based company are sprouting up across the US, sparking alarm and bipartisan, citizen-driven campaigns as the new technology emerges as a 2026 midterm campaign issue. While politicians hedge and local officials rush to sign contracts, community volunteers attempt to address an issue with major implications for future generations. But it might be too late.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbefa0a6-cf0d-11f1-8363-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/flock-main.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbefa0a6-cf0d-11f1-8363-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/flock-main.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a460651a-cf0e-11f1-9b74-69cc4d2fd839</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:26:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbefa0a6-cf0d-11f1-8363-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/flock-main.png">© David Goldman, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ballon d’Or winner Harry Kane delivers emotional acceptance speech</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ballon-d-or-winner-harry-kane-delivers-emotional-acceptance-speech</link><description>
Harry Kane became the first Englishman in 25 years to win the Ballon d’Or on Monday. Kane scored 73 goals for club and country last campaign and smashed scoring records at the World Cup, where he captained England to a third-place finish.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88b0c438-d1ff-11f1-8eeb-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/minikane.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88b0c438-d1ff-11f1-8eeb-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/minikane.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac880998-d1ff-11f1-b96e-f143e24026c3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 12:20:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>American rapper Macklemore begins 'Free Palestine' tour</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-american-rapper-macklemore-begins-free-palestine-tour</link><description>
The American rapper Macklemore vows to speak out loudly against the war in Gaza. He started his "Free Palestine" tour in Ireland, one of Europe's most pro-Palestinian countries.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6efefc4e-b175-11f1-b1a1-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/8022933136001w.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6efefc4e-b175-11f1-b1a1-3ff9dda05487/w:1024/p:16x9/8022933136001w.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6b658b26-d1f9-11f1-9197-8770ad4b4b1e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:57:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US midterms: Trump escalates anti-Muslim attacks against Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-us-midterms-trump-escalates-anti-muslim-attacks-against-democratic-senate-candidate-abdul-el-sayed</link><description>
As the US midterm elections approach, the Michigan Senate race is splitting communities. Trump is escalating anti-Muslim attacks against Abdul El-Sayed, the Michigan Democratic Senate candidate, who could become the first Muslim senator in US history.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0dc0cb6-bcb0-11f1-aaa4-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26220008573430.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0dc0cb6-bcb0-11f1-aaa4-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26220008573430.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">42404818-d1f8-11f1-9024-55ea83e65116</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:56:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Sudan: One year after the fall of El-Fasher</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-sudan-one-year-after-the-fall-of-el-fasher</link><description>
It has been one year since the fall of El-Fasher in Sudan, a city in North Darfur, which was captured by the Rapid Support Forces. At least 6,000 civilians were killed by rebel troops as they entered this strategic city.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/406be9ce-d1ea-11f1-b8bf-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-214358-214533-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/406be9ce-d1ea-11f1-b8bf-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261026-214358-214533-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">46063f9c-d1ea-11f1-80ae-350239596e70</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:46:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>South Africa suspends asylum applications after recent unrest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-south-africa-suspends-asylum-applications-after-recent-unrest</link><description>
Tensions in South Africa over anti-migrant protests have left in limbo many who were counting on following the rules to sort out their paperwork and status in the country. Calls for a crackdown on foreigners, particularly undocumented migrants, have sometimes spiralled into murder. In response to the unrest, the government suspended the asylum application process.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e080c762-d1f0-11f1-a0e1-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3a9aa983.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e080c762-d1f0-11f1-a0e1-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3a9aa983.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da3c8bea-d1ee-11f1-a77e-13226d517053</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:37:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French government concessions to students 'tactically shrewd' but risk creating new set of problems</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/french-government-concessions-to-students-tactically-shrewd-but-risk-creating-new-set-of-problems</link><description>
Oliver Farry welcomes Oliver Davis, Professor and Head of the Department of French at University College Cork. According to Professor Davis, the government's handling of the student protests reflects a combination of "tactical confusion" and an inadequate response to deeper structural problems. Davis cautions the concessions offered to secondary school students merely "scratch the surface." Meanwhile, France's widening protest movement has extended well beyond the classroom, drawing in the Yellow Vests, trade unions and people from across French society, amid mounting frustrations over public services and the rising cost of living.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4965e618-d1f6-11f1-82af-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-081020-081854-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4965e618-d1f6-11f1-82af-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-081020-081854-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f1dc56c-d1f6-11f1-9959-adfc90f53f15</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:35:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Algeria to deploy army units to Niger to protect economic interests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-algeria-deploys-army-units-to-niger-to-protect-economic-interests</link><description>
Algeria will send army units to Niger to ​protect energy and economic interests, according to a statement from the presidency on Monday (October 26). Algeria's Parliament held an emergency vote on Sunday on what would be Algeria's first such foreign mission since 1973.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ddd4cfa-d1f0-11f1-98ed-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a1bc55d9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ddd4cfa-d1f0-11f1-98ed-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a1bc55d9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ce0aefa-d1ed-11f1-8f3f-3f3d8cf5602f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:28:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>French protests: Student union leaders vow to keep mobilising</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-french-protests-student-union-leaders-vow-to-keep-mobilising</link><description>
In France, after weeks of student unrest, the government announced new school measures. Student union leaders said it's a first step but vowed to keep mobilising as they expected further proposals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be12ccb2-d1f4-11f1-8ee4-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-755f6a50.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be12ccb2-d1f4-11f1-8ee4-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-755f6a50.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">64966680-d1f4-11f1-99c4-b198ab47fb28</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:18:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iraqi court sentences six French nationals to life for IS group membership</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-iraqi-court-sentences-six-french-nationals-to-life-for-is-group-membership</link><description>
Six French men were sentenced to life in prison by an Iraqi court on Tuesday for membership of the Islamic State (IS) group, according to a source. They are ​among ‌47 French IS group suspects transferred from ⁠detention facilities in Syria to Iraq last year under an arrangement coordinated by US forces and Iraqi authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4cd4b7c2-d1f4-11f1-9de6-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-05T101214Z-1232127138-RC2YWNAFNRTE-RTRMADP-3-IRAQ-USA-COALITION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4cd4b7c2-d1f4-11f1-9de6-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-05T101214Z-1232127138-RC2YWNAFNRTE-RTRMADP-3-IRAQ-USA-COALITION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8b1d30a-d1f5-11f1-9f39-7ba635be4210</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:16:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4cd4b7c2-d1f4-11f1-9de6-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-05T101214Z-1232127138-RC2YWNAFNRTE-RTRMADP-3-IRAQ-USA-COALITION.jpg">© Ahmed Saad, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Israeli election: Fragile co-existence between residents in Jewish-Arab town of Lod</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261027-israeli-election-fragile-co-existence-between-residents-in-jewish-arab-town-of-lod</link><description>
As Israelis head to the polls this Tuesday, among those voting are 2 million Palestinian citizens of Israel, some of whom live in mixed Jewish-Arab towns. One of them, Lod, has long been seen as symbolic of this coexistence. However in 2021 the town was the scene of violent clashes, whose consequences are still being felt. FRANCE 24's Stéphane Amar, Sandra Lederer and Josh Vardey report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4515330-d158-11f1-842c-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ISRAEL-LOD-COEXISTENCE-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4515330-d158-11f1-842c-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-ISRAEL-LOD-COEXISTENCE-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">425f12b2-d161-11f1-9c76-d7ca4cf6da32</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:14:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Josh VARDEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Chad hosts hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees as regional humanitarian crisis extends</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-chad-hosts-hundreds-of-thousands-of-sudanese-refugees-as-regional-humanitarian-crisis-extends</link><description>
Sudan’s war is spilling over into Chad. A drone strike killed at least four people last week in the border town of Bamina, and hundreds of thousands of Sudanese refugees have crossed over in search of safety. Many of those who survived the massacre in El Fasher are still deeply traumatised. FRANCE 24's correspondent Harold Girard has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b861376e-d1ee-11f1-b904-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4e39aeb0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b861376e-d1ee-11f1-b904-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4e39aeb0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">149bffd0-d1ec-11f1-bdfd-7d7dd1394a0b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:13:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Syria slams deadly Jordan strikes as ‘unacceptable’ breach of airspace</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-syria-slams-deadly-jordan-strikes-as-unacceptable-breach-of-airspace</link><description>
Syria's foreign ministry on Tuesday condemned Jordanian strikes in southern Syria in retaliation for a deadly church attack in the kingdom last week that Amman linked to militants operating across the border. Syria said the strikes killed seven ⁠people, including three children and a woman. Jordan said it regretted the civilian casualties.
 
 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d31e64f6-d1f2-11f1-96c1-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4JD7KE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d31e64f6-d1f2-11f1-96c1-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4JD7KE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c570d564-d1f2-11f1-88a1-6b707fbacb87</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:02:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d31e64f6-d1f2-11f1-96c1-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D4JD7KE.jpg">© Bakr Alkasem, AFP </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Jordan launches airstrikes in Syria after church attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/jordan-launches-airstrikes-in-syria-after-church-attack</link><description>
Jordan carried out airstrikes Monday (October 27) evening against armed groups in Syria in retaliation for Friday’s attack on a Greek Orthodox Church in the southern Jordanian city of Karak that killed nine people, the Jordanian air force said in a statement. Syrian authorities said at least six people were killed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d399f3dc-d1f2-11f1-b5c5-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-101506-101623-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d399f3dc-d1f2-11f1-b5c5-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-101506-101623-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8f1695a-d1f2-11f1-946e-030292f08554</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:59:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Palestinians in West Bank fear further escalation of violence if Netanyahu remains PM</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/palestinians-in-west-bank-fear-further-escalation-of-violence-if-netanyahu-remains-pm</link><description>
Ramallah residents say they hope to see Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lose power in elections. "Netanyahu remaining in power means that there will be a clash, a build-up of tension and an explosion in the region", says one resident. Israel has committed the crime against humanity of "extermination" in the West Bank, while continuing to commit "genocide" against Palestinians in the Gaza Strip, United Nations-mandated investigators said Monday (October 27).
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/411612b6-d1f2-11f1-ab2e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-101255-101430-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/411612b6-d1f2-11f1-ab2e-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-101255-101430-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4679462e-d1f2-11f1-a52b-7ffae517304d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:50:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israelis vote in first national election since October 7 attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-first-national-election-since-october-7-attack</link><description>
Israelis are voting in a pivotal election Tuesday (October 27) as their country wrestles with unresolved wars, continues to reel from Hamas' 2023 attack and is deeply divided over the character of the state and the right person to lead it. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more from the ground. He spoke with voters.
