In Azerbaijan, a new government ban on hijab in schools has provoked rare public protests. The ban prohibits clothing deemed "incompatible with the secular principles of general education". While it does not mention Islamic hijab, girls and teachers wearing hijab have been turned away from schools. The measure has sparked tensions in a country where 96% of the population is Muslim.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17098974-d1ef-11f1-89d4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/azerbaidjan-fond-EN.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17098974-d1ef-11f1-89d4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/azerbaidjan-fond-EN.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">84e28342-d1ef-11f1-9f38-5b52ec707215</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:16:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu's political survival on the line as Israel heads to the polls</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-s-political-survival-on-the-line-as-israel-heads-to-the-polls</link><description>
